  <div class="seo-answer"><strong>Direct answer:</strong> ADHD and autism assessment at Mind Grace covers children, adolescents, and adults. It considers development, communication, attention, behaviour, learning, sensory experiences, health, and everyday functioning across home, school, and work settings.</div>
<main id="main-content" class="seo-page"><section class="seo-hero"><p class="seo-kicker">Neurodevelopmental assessment</p><h1>ADHD and autism questions deserve context</h1><p class="seo-lead">Assessment considers development, communication, attention, behaviour, learning, sensory experiences, health, and everyday functioning across settings.</p><div class="seo-actions"><a class="btn" href="/assessments">Assessment information</a><a class="btn btn-outline" href="/child-development">Child development</a></div></section><section class="seo-section"><h2>What an assessment may include</h2><div class="seo-grid"><article class="seo-card"><h3>History and observation</h3><p>Developmental history, family observations, school feedback, and the person’s own experience may be gathered.</p></article><article class="seo-card"><h3>Structured tools</h3><p>Questionnaires or tests may be used when clinically appropriate; no single checklist gives a diagnosis.</p></article><article class="seo-card"><h3>Recommendations</h3><p>The outcome may include practical strategies, school guidance, follow-up, or referral.</p></article></div><div class="seo-note"><strong>Important:</strong> Online content cannot diagnose ADHD or autism. Assessment scope, duration, and report format are confirmed before booking.</div></section>    
